<title>SPAIN: Spain Feb industrial production fell 0.3 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Spain Feb industrial production fell 0.3 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Statistics Institute gave the following provisional figures (percentage change):</p>
<p> INDUSTRIAL PRODUCTION		  FEB 97    JAN 96  FEB 96</p>
<p> Yr/yr					-0.3	  2.8R    0.9</p>
<p> Avg yr to date against yr ago	 1.3	  2.9    -0.2</p>
<p> Calendar-adjusted yr/yr		 1.9	  5.0R   -1.2</p>
<p>The INE gave the following breakdown on a year-year basis:</p>
<p> Energy				     -8.7	 3.1	  0.0</p>
<p> Chemicals				  -2.6	 8.6	 -3.5</p>
<p> Precision tools			  -1.4	12.1	 -8.9</p>
<p> Other manufacturing industry	  6.7	 4.7	 -5.6</p>
<p> Consumer goods			    4.5	 6.5	 -5.1</p>
<p> Capital goods			     3.0	 9.2	 -8.2</p>
<p> Intermediate goods		     -5.0	 7.2	 -4.5</p>
<p>NOTE - Monthly variation is year-on-year. Latest two months' figures are provisional.  </p>
<p>The INE gave the following breakdown of calendar-adjusted figures, which take into account differences in the number of working days (percentage change year on year):</p>
<p>					     FEB 97     JAN 96   FEB 96</p>
<p> General index			    1.9	   5.0R   -1.2</p>
<p> Consumption goods			7.3	   7.9R    8.2</p>
<p> Capital goods			    6.1	   9.8R    9.7</p>
<p> Intermediate goods		    -3.5	   1.9     1.9</p>
<p>-- Madrid Newsroom, + 341 585 8340</p>
</text>
